        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: North Koʻolaupoko, Kāneʻohe, Oʻahu, Hawaii, United States\n- Topics: Place names, Hawaiian etymology\n\nFacts:\n- North Koʻolaupoko is an area in the City and County of Honolulu, Hawaii, United States, on the island of Oʻahu.\n- According to an ancient Hawaiian story, the place name Kāneʻohe originated when a local woman compared her husband's cruelty to the sharp edge of cutting bamboo, leading to the meaning \"Bamboo man.\"",
